  m_Name: Q6
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HistoricalQuestionData
  questionID: Q6
  questionText: The story "The Legend of Betel and Areca" explains the origin of
    what custom in Vietnam?
  answers:
  - The custom of chewing betel
  - The custom of wrapping banh chung
  - The custom of blackening teeth
  - Ancestor worship
  correctAnswerIndex: 0
  answerFeedbacks:
  - Exactly! The legend of Betel and Areca praises brotherhood and marital love and
    explains the custom of using betel and areca in wedding ceremonies.
  - "Wrong! Banh chung and banh giay (another type of sticky rice cake) are associated
    with the legend of Lang Li\xEAu during the Hung King era."
  - Wrong! The custom of blackening teeth is an ancient beauty practice, not originating
    from the legend of Betel and Areca.
  - Wrong! Ancestor worship is a core belief of the Vietnamese people, not a custom
    originating from this story.
  difficultyTier: 1
